WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.930
Because Montessori is grounded in prepared environments and concrete

1
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:08.170
sensory exploration rather than traditional grade level textbooks,

2
00:00:08.409 --> 00:00:13.039
aligning this philosophy with public charter requirements can pose challenges.

3
00:00:13.399 --> 00:00:15.550
Collecting work samples can be an obstacle.

4
00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:16.610
Traditional.

5
00:00:16.754 --> 00:00:20.534
Paper and pencil worksheets are rare in an authentic Montessori home,

6
00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:24.114
making standard paperwork samples difficult to provide.

7
00:00:24.514 --> 00:00:27.504
Families may want to order specialty wooden manipulatives,

8
00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:28.745
sensory materials,

9
00:00:28.954 --> 00:00:33.435
and multi-age items that can be difficult to find in school ordering guidelines.

10
00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:37.909
Montessori prioritizes a child's natural sensitive periods,

11
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:41.029
meaning a student may focus intensely on one

12
00:00:41.029 --> 00:00:43.669
subject for weeks while setting others aside,

13
00:00:43.909 --> 00:00:46.270
creating gaps in traditional monthly pacing

14
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:49.220
guides and grade level standards expectations.

15
00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:53.689
This can also make it difficult to align with a work sample collection schedule.

16
00:00:54.029 --> 00:00:54.040
Because

17
00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.740
Montessori relies on self-correcting materials and intrinsic motivation,

18
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.860
students are not always exposed to traditional testing formats,

19
00:01:02.869 --> 00:01:05.750
which can lead to anxiety during required assessments.